{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games","id":927600,"title":"Applying Vampire's Health-as-Conditions to other games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-07T07:06:04-07:00","id":927600,"title":"Applying Vampire's Health-as-Conditions to other games","content":"So I'm not just a huge fan of Conditions, I'm also a big fan of how CofD's dice system is almost without-fail agnostic of the # of successes. Whether you get 1 success or 4, it doesn't matter, so every result is either a Dramatic Failure, Failure, Success, or Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> Except in combat.<br /> <br /> Now, for the most part this isn't a huge deal to me: combat's been made pretty quick thanks to stuff like Down &amp; Dirty and making weapons add to damage rather than the roll, but doing this one last change sounds like an interesting idea to me. Has anybody tried porting it over to other games? What about games like Mummy, where filling all of your health boxes with Aggravated isn't even a surefire way to keep 'em down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:38:38-07:00","id":927609,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking about how to port health boxes over to the Conditions system last week, but I didn't know Vampire had already done it. Where are those rules? Or sum them up here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:47:54-07:00","id":927612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=927609#post927609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking about how to port health boxes over to the Conditions system last week, but I didn't know Vampire had already done it. Where are those rules? Or sum them up here?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in the Storytelling chapter of Requiem 2E (p 277). Summed up they're pretty easy:<br /> <br /> By default, you may take the Dying Condition when injured.<br /> If your Stam + Size is greater than 3, you can take the Incapacitated Condition when you're injured.<br /> If your Stam + Size is greater than 6, you can also take the Maimed Condition when you're injured.<br /> For every 2 above 6 your Stam + Size is, you may take a Bruised Condition when you're injured.<br /> <br /> Each one's Resolution is related to healing times and spending resources to Heal, or getting medical attention. Kind of similar to how Fate Core handles Consequences, but more codified.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:50:46-07:00","id":927616,"title":"","content":"I'd be surprised if Hurt Locker doesn't have a hack for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:38:55-07:00","id":927634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=927616#post927616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be surprised if Hurt Locker doesn't have a hack for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does!<br /> <br /> It's pretty much exactly the same, and <i>still</i> doesn't account for the Poisoned Tilt.<br /> <hr /><br /> Just drop Size from HL calculations and have attacks deal 1 damage on a S, and 2 damage on an ES.<br /> <br /> Then let people take Tilts in place of damage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T10:53:38-07:00","id":927682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=927634#post927634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does!<br /> <br /> It's pretty much exactly the same, and <i>still</i> doesn't account for the Poisoned Tilt.<br /> <hr /><br /> Just drop Size from HL calculations and have attacks deal 1 damage on a S, and 2 damage on an ES.<br /> <br /> Then let people take Tilts in place of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would you let people take up a maximum number of Tilts equal to their HL and <i>also </i>have that many Health Conditions? Or just Tilts? I was picturing like how Fate Core has both a Stress Track and Consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:54:11-07:00","id":927746,"title":"","content":"As long as you only use Tilts that people would normally suffer for attacks, fights are going to reach a natural end long before they usually do. Block 1 damage with the temporary version of the Tilt, 2 damage with the version that needs surgery to fix.<br /> <br /> So if your attacker scores an Exceptional Success, you're probably out of the fight... unless you &quot;sacrifice&quot; an arm blocking the axe that was going for your face. Either you just banged it badly and still got gashed by the axe, or it mangled your arm pretty badly.<br /> <br /> It's a way to stop people with Stamina 2 from dying in a solid hit or two.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:26:27-07:00","id":929002,"title":"","content":"It will be in Hurt Locker. My group tried it out in a Demon one-shot, and didn't like it, and it didn't seem like the fight was going faster, actually it seemed much slower than the damage that would have happened if we hadn't used this system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T01:15:44-07:00","id":929109,"title":"","content":"There are quite a few optional alternative systems coming up in Hurt Locker. One that might fit what you want is similar to Health-as-Conditions system, but substitutes specific Conditions and Tilts based on how the damage occurs, instead if the standard health Conditions from Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T19:22:21-07:00","id":934242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=927746#post927746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you only use Tilts that people would normally suffer for attacks, fights are going to reach a natural end long before they usually do. Block 1 damage with the temporary version of the Tilt, 2 damage with the version that needs surgery to fix.<br /> <br /> So if your attacker scores an Exceptional Success, you're probably out of the fight... unless you &quot;sacrifice&quot; an arm blocking the axe that was going for your face. Either you just banged it badly and still got gashed by the axe, or it mangled your arm pretty badly.<br /> <br /> It's a way to stop people with Stamina 2 from dying in a solid hit or two.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How would this account for armor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T19:47:16-07:00","id":934248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934242#post934242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would this account for armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Armor removes successes; that's how I'd handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:33:48-07:00","id":934334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934248#post934248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Armor removes successes; that's how I'd handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, neat.<br /> <br /> Stealing this for my To The Strongest chronicle set in Corinth, it suddenly makes magic damage spells far more terrifying, since they inflict (Potency) damage. And a Potency of 5 in a place where everyone has no higher than 5 health levels is pretty terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 07-20-2016, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T08:43:47-07:00","id":934509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934334#post934334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, neat.<br /> <br /> Stealing this for my To The Strongest chronicle set in Corinth, it suddenly makes magic damage spells far more terrifying, since they inflict (Potency) damage. And a Potency of 5 in a place where everyone has no higher than 5 health levels is pretty terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it would still deal 1 or 2 damage under this system. It's just youi have much more flexibility in terms of range and what Tilts your opponent has to take if they want to offset the damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:53:38-07:00","id":934662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934509#post934509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it would still deal 1 or 2 damage under this system. It's just youi have much more flexibility in terms of range and what Tilts your opponent has to take if they want to offset the damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, that would streamline the magic system a lot.<br /> <br /> Under this paradigm, you would actually have Withstand ratings for damage spells, which I totally should have thought of when I made that post.<br /> <br /> So I take it that under this system, the purpose of Weapon Modifier is to add successes in case you hit? Or are they done away with entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:42:22-07:00","id":934692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934662#post934662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm, that would streamline the magic system a lot.<br /> <br /> Under this paradigm, you would actually have Withstand ratings for damage spells, which I totally should have thought of when I made that post.<br /> <br /> So I take it that under this system, the purpose of Weapon Modifier is to add successes in case you hit? Or are they done away with entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weapon modifiers actually are a bonus to your successes already, so that stays the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:13:51-07:00","id":934699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934692#post934692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weapon modifiers actually are a bonus to your successes already, so that stays the same.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wonderful, I guessed right.<br /> <br /> So a battle under this system would look like this:<br /> <br /> Sisyphus and Lysandra decide to fight, for some arbitrary reason:<br /> <br /> Sisyphus is a Blood Potency 3 vampire with Vigor 3, Resilience 4 and Celerity 3 because he is made of fite, while Lysandra is a Gnosis 1 mage with Forces 3, Prime 1, Life 2.<br /> <br /> Lysandra is also a Prelate of Fury using your version of that Prelacy.<br /> <br /> Lysandra has three health levels and Sisyphus has seven due to Resilience.<br /> <br /> They both roll Initiative: Lysandra gets 4, and Sisyphus gets 9.<br /> <br /> Sisyphus rolls to attack, using a dice pool of 9, reduced to 5 by Lysandra's Defense, he gets 1 success, which is increased to 3 by his Makhaira, dealing a single point of damage to Lysandra, bringing her down to two health levels.<br /> <br /> Lysandra chooses to spend her turn on activating her Forces Armor.<br /> <br /> Sisyphus attacks her again, rolling a total of 3 successes, reduced to 0 by Lysandra's Mage Armor.<br /> <br /> Lysandra starts casting a Forces spell to burn him to cinders with a touch. She uses only the Yantra of her Prelacy for a +2 bonus, hoping to finish this quickly. <br /> <br /> She gains 2 successes, increased by 3 due to her Potency, gaining her 5 successes.<br /> <br /> Sisyphus chooses to accept the damage and takes two levels of aggravated.<br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:44:39-07:00","id":934715,"title":"","content":"That looks about right. Probably needs some tweaking, but it's workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T15:18:17-07:00","id":934726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934715#post934715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That looks about right. Probably needs some tweaking, but it's workable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It probably does need some changing, given that combat magic really doesn't feel worth it.<br /> <br /> You take penalties due to Potency, and then you take penalties due to Defense, which honestly makes combat magic worse than just using a gun or punching a dude.<br /> <br /> Normally this was countered by the fact that you could pump the damage to ridiculous levels by just increasing Potency to lol-worthy levels, but here it isn't quite like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T15:40:45-07:00","id":934738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934726#post934726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It probably does need some changing, given that combat magic really doesn't feel worth it.<br /> <br /> You take penalties due to Potency, and then you take penalties due to Defense, which honestly makes combat magic worse than just using a gun or punching a dude.<br /> <br /> Normally this was countered by the fact that you could pump the damage to ridiculous levels by just increasing Potency to lol-worthy levels, but here it isn't quite like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Just give everyone Fast Spells for free, even if they don't have Time \u2022 or Firearms \u2022\u2022 (I never <i>got</i> the Firearms prereq).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T16:25:39-07:00","id":934768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927600-applying-vampire-s-health-as-conditions-to-other-games?p=934738#post934738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly? Just give everyone Fast Spells for free, even if they don't have Time \u2022 or Firearms \u2022\u2022 (I never <i>got</i> the Firearms prereq).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I'm not the only one who uses that houserule.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Firearms prereq is dumb.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T20:21:25-07:00","id":934872,"title":"","content":"Alright, so let me map how this works in my brain,<br /> <br /> <u>Turn 1</u><br /> So a detective with size 5 and Stamina 2 is ambushed by a mob gunman in the hallway outside of an office he was about to break into. The gunman fires, and with no defense or armor, the detective is hit.<br /> <br /> With 7 points he can only take the <b>Maimed Condition</b> and the <b>Incapacitated Condition</b>. Being has he doesn't want to be Incapacitated, he takes the <b>Maimed Condition</b>. All his actions suffer a -2 penalty, including initiative. In addition his speed is halved.<br /> <br /> The Detective, on his turn draws and shoots the gunman, spending a willpower and aiming for the gunman's hand; hoping for an <b>Arm Wrack</b> tilt(-6 penalty total; with the -2 for the <b>Maimed Condition</b> plus the -4 aiming penalty). Remarkably, he hits, forcing the gunman to drop his gun.With Stamina + Size of 8 the gunman can and does take the <b>Bruised Condition</b> in addition to the <b>Arm Wrack</b> tilt. The gunman takes a -1 penalty to initiative and all instant actions. As well he takes a -2 penalties that involve manual dexterity with his off hand(like using a gun). Most importantly, the gunman drops his gun.<br /> <br /> <u>Turn 2</u><br /> The gunman, now disarmed but not out draws a knife with his off hand and charges the detective. Not having enough actions to attack he ends his turn in melee range of the detective, knife drawn.<br /> <br /> The detective, not wanting to shoot in melee combat, decides to improvise; using his heavy revolver as a improvised weapon he slams the weapon into the head of the gunman the moment he gets in arms reach. The gunman has defense 5, the ST rules the heavy revolver is close enough to a sap to use it as a general guideline and uses its stat block. With strength 3 and weaponry 3(-1 penalty for improvised weapon), he spends a willpower and an all out attack to make sure he gets over the gunman's defense(made worse as the <b>Maimed Condition</b> applies a -2 penalty to this roll). With 3 dice he lands 1 success. Slamming the weapon into the head of the gunman.<br /> <br /> With his only <b>Bruised Condition</b> used, the gunman is forced to take the <b>Maimed Condition</b>. Really should of brought some armor.<br /> <br /> <u>Turn 3</u><br /> <i>Recap</i><br /> The Detective has:<ul><li><b>Maimed Condition</b>; -2 penalty to all rolls and initiative and halved speed.</li> </ul>The Gunman has:<ul><li><b>Bruised Condition</b>; -1 penalty to initiative and all instant actions.</li> <li><b>Arm Wrack</b>; -2 penalty to rolls requiring manual dexterity in your off hand.</li> <li><b>Maimed Condition</b>; -2 penalty to all rolls and initiative and halved speed.</li> </ul>The Gunman, with little other choice, tries to stab the detective in the gut. His normal dice pool is Strength 2 + weaponry(Knife specialty) 3 = 6 dice. With his three conditions, he applies a -5 penalty to his attack. He spends a willpower to raise his dice pool up to 4. He gains 1 success.<br /> <br /> The Detective, with no defense or armor takes the <b>Incapacitated Condition</b>. It levy's no penalty, but every turn he must roll stamina or fall unconscious.<br /> <br /> The detective rolls, spending his last willpower to add 3 dice to his stamina roll. he gains a success so he doesn't get knocked out this turn. its now or never. He attacks. Unfortunately, he knows the gunman has 5 defense, his attack pool is 5, and he has a -2 penalty thanks to the <b>Maimed Condition</b>. his attack is a chance die, but he rolls it anyway. He fails his roll, the gunman easily deflecting his blow.<br /> <br /> <u>Turn 4 and so on...</u><br /> The gunman attacks, this time at a detective with his full 5 defense. he rolls a chance die.<br /> <br /> The Detective rolls to stay up, if he wins he attacks, he can take any penalty he wants on the roll; as long as the gunman doesn't drop his defenses the attack will be a chance die. If he ever fails his stamina roll he goes down.<br /> <br /> Does this sound about right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:21:21-07:00","id":936239,"title":"","content":"The great thing about this system is that it makes Resilience actually worth having.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}